cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fepdmc-toolkit: source patches, run tools, statistics and a diagram compiler for first-principles electron-phonon diagrammatic Monte Carlo"
message: "If you use this software, cite it and the FEP-DMC paper by Luo, Park and Bernardi."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wong
    given-names: Kawa
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/DarrenWongKaWa/fepdmc-toolkit"
abstract: >
  Tools for the FEP-DMC code of Luo, Park and Bernardi: opt-in fixes for
  defects in the native external-phonon updates, exact Monte Carlo moves,
  a Docker run driver, an end-to-end exactness check and a pooled ratio
  estimator; source adapters for a phonon-frequency refresh (C0) and for
  exact-corrected delayed acceptance in the swap update (P1); statistics
  helpers; and an experimental compiler from fixed-order electron-phonon
  diagram families to an exact delayed-acceptance kernel and generated Fortran.
keywords:
  - diagrammatic Monte Carlo
  - electron-phonon
  - polaron
  - FEP-DMC
  - delayed acceptance
references:
  - type: article
    title: "First-principles diagrammatic Monte Carlo for electron-phonon interactions and polarons"
    authors:
      - family-names: Luo
        given-names: Yao
      - family-names: Park
        given-names: Jinsoo
      - family-names: Bernardi
        given-names: Marco
    journal: Nature Physics
    year: 2025
    volume: "21"
    pages: "1275"
    doi: "10.1038/s41567-025-02954-1"
